WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.888
Idea. Every house needs its own address, so post arrives at the right door. Every device on a network needs one too. An I P address is a number that identifies a device.

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:30.337
An I P version four address is written as four denary numbers, each from zero to two hundred and fifty-five, separated by dots. Each number fits in eight bits. For example, one hundred and ninety-two is one one zero zero, zero zero zero zero.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:43.422
So I P version four uses thirty-two bits, which gives about four point three billion addresses. The number of connected devices grew so much that I P version four was running out.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:51.517
An I P version six address is written as eight groups of four hexadecimal digits, separated by colons.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:59.512
Each hexadecimal digit stands for exactly four bits, because four bits give sixteen values, from zero to F.

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:12.779
Method. Here is the whole picture. I P version four: four parts of eight bits, thirty-two bits. I P version six: eight groups of sixteen bits, one hundred and twenty-eight bits.

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:26.159
So the method is: decide the version, count the groups and digits, then multiply. Four digits times four bits is sixteen bits a group. Eight groups times sixteen is one hundred and twenty-eight.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:43.042
Worked example. Here is a real question from Paper 1 in June 2024. Marie's phone has this address. Describe the relationship between its structure and the total number of bits needed to store it. It is worth three marks.

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:51.587
Count the groups between the colons: there are eight. Each group has four hex digits, so there are thirty-two hex digits in total.

00:01:52.150 --> 00:02:10.698
Each hex digit needs four bits, so each group is sixteen bits. Eight groups times sixteen bits is one hundred and twenty-eight bits. Check: thirty-two digits times four is also one hundred and twenty-eight. This explanation is by olevels.com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:21.516
Common mistake. A common mistake is saying each hex digit is eight bits. One hex digit is four bits. A pair of hex digits makes eight bits.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:28.154
Another mistake is counting the colons. There are seven colons, but eight groups. Count the groups.

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:44.708
Your turn. Now you try. A device has the address ten dot zero dot twenty-five dot two hundred. How many bits are used to store it? Show your working. Then say why I P version six was introduced. Pause here and work it out.

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:54.391
Answer. It has dots and denary numbers, so it is I P version four. Four numbers, each eight bits, gives thirty-two bits.

00:02:54.950 --> 00:03:06.981
I P version six was introduced because so many devices came online that I P version four was running out of addresses. Its one hundred and twenty-eight bits give vastly more.

00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:21.789
Remember the method: dots mean four times eight, thirty-two bits. Colons mean eight times sixteen, one hundred and twenty-eight bits. And one hex digit is four bits. Now try the practice questions for this type.
